{
  "id": "middleware",
  "title": "Middleware",
  "notApplicable": ["hpp"],
  "summary": "Middleware is code that runs around every request. One middleware file at the project root runs before every request and again after the response. It can reject a request, or change or replace the response of the controller. Who may call a route is decided by the route itself (`Public`, `SignedIn`, `Allow(Role)`) and the one identity provider, not by middleware. C++ has no tab here, because C++ gets root middleware in a later step: a C++ project writes its middleware in another Yon language for now (ADR 0099).",
  "group": "Yon server",
